@title Observability Stack for 2027
@subtitle Comparison for the budget meeting
@author SRE team, Copperleaf Insurance

We run 340 hosts, ingest about 2.1 TB of logs per month, and have 14 engineers on call. This page compares three options for the 2027 observability stack.

# Comparison table

table = Option,Setup effort,Alerting,Log search,Lock-in,Annual cost; Datadog,low,excellent,excellent,high,"$412,000"; Grafana Cloud,low,good,good,medium,"$236,000"; Self-hosted,high,good,fair,low,"$148,000 plus 1.5 engineers"

# Three-year cost

data cum = year,Datadog,Grafana Cloud,Self-hosted incl staff; 2027,412,236,418; 2028,865,496,706; 2029,1363,782,1004
chart line cum x=year y=Datadog,Grafana Cloud,Self-hosted incl staff unit=$K title="Cumulative cost, thousands of dollars"

# Pros and cons

### Datadog

- Pro: excellent alerting and log search.
- Pro: low setup effort.
- Con: high lock-in.
- Con: the highest annual cost.

### Grafana Cloud

- Pro: low setup effort.
- Pro: dashboards stay portable.
- Con: log search is good, not excellent.
- Con: medium lock-in.

### Self-hosted

- Pro: low lock-in, and the lowest license cost.
- Con: high setup effort.
- Con: fair log search.
- Con: needs about 1.5 engineers to run.

# Recommendation

Grafana Cloud. It is the cheapest option once staff time is counted, and it keeps our dashboards portable.

! The Datadog quote expires on 2026-11-30. Self-hosted assumes we can hire the 1.5 engineers, which is not yet approved.
